{
  "generated_text": "To round \\(\\frac{4}{7}\\) to the nearest tenth, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the fraction to a decimal:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{7} \\approx 0.5714285714285714\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the digit in the tenths place:**\n   The tenths place is the first digit to the right of the decimal point. For \\(0.5714285714285714\\), the digit in the tenths place is \\(5\\).\n\n3. **Identify the digit in the hundredths place:**\n   The hundredths place is the second digit to the right of the decimal point. For \\(0.5714285714285714\\), the digit in the hundredths place is \\(7\\).\n\n4. **Determine whether to round up or down:**\n   - If the digit in the hundredths place is 5 or greater, we round the digit in the tenths place up by one.\n   - If the digit in the hundredths place is less than 5, we leave the digit in the tenths place as it is.\n\n   Here, the digit in the hundredths place is \\(7\\), which is greater than \\(5\\). Therefore, we round the digit in the tenths place (which is \\(5\\)) up by one.\n\n5. **Perform the rounding:**\n   - The digit in the tenths place is \\(5\\), and rounding it up by one gives \\(6\\).\n\n6. **Form the rounded number:**\n   - The digits to the right of the tenths place become zero, so \\(0.5714285714285714\\) rounded to the nearest tenth is \\(0.6\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.6}\n\\]",
